{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobenius_positivity_filter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobenius_positivity_filter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.BigOperators","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.DeriveFintype","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobenius_positivity_filter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobenius_positivity_filter","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L165-L187","doc":"**Frobenius positivity filter — corrected, proved (manuscript part (ii)).**\n\n*Conditional on the sign-mechanism characterisation* `hchar` (a\nconfiguration is excluded ⟺ its per-factor sign-pattern `signOf c` has odd\ntotal parity — the Hoefsmit spectator-factor structure), exactly `2^{A-1}`\nof the `2^A` sign-patterns are excluded, for `A ≥ 1`.\n\nThe hypothesis `hchar` carries the *mechanism* (the physical input); the\n`2^{A-1}` count is then **derived** from `parity_odd_card` (no `sorry`).\nThis replaces the previous unconditional statement over the `4^A`\nconfiguration space, which was false for generic `ProductData` (see the\naudit doc referenced above). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:frobenius-positivity-filter","label":"prop:frobenius-positivity-filter","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/frobenius-positivity-filter.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.parity_odd_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.parity_odd_card","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L119-L163","doc":"**Parity count (provable core).** Exactly half — `2^{A-1}` — of the `2^A`\nper-factor sign-patterns `Fin A → ZMod 2` have odd total parity\n`∑ᵢ sᵢ = 1`.\n\nProof: drop the last coordinate.  Any tail `t : Fin (A-1) → ZMod 2` extends\nto a *unique* odd-parity vector (the head is forced to `1 − ∑ t`), so the\nodd-parity set is in bijection with `Fin (A-1) → ZMod 2`, which has\ncardinality `2^{A-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.excludedConfigs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.excludedConfigs","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L101-L104","doc":"The set of **excluded** (non-Frobenius-positive) configurations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobeniusPositive_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobeniusPositive_iff","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L92-L99","doc":"**Characterisation (definitional).** Frobenius-positivity is exactly\nthe conjunction of parent- and daughter-product non-negativity.  This\nis the manuscript's part (i); it holds by definition of the predicate\n(it is *not* projected from a context field — the predicate is defined\nby this conjunction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPositive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPositive","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L87-L90","doc":"A configuration is **Frobenius-positive** when both the parent and the\ndaughter mass products are non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.ProductData.daughterProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.ProductData.daughterProd","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Daughter product `m_{e,dau}(c) = ∏ₘ G_{n'ₘ}(cₘ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.ProductData.parentProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.ProductData.parentProd","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Parent product `m_{e,par}(c) = ∏ₘ G_{nₘ}(cₘ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.ProductData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.ProductData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.ProductData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.ProductData","kind":"structure","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L76-L85","doc":"The parent / daughter mass products are real-valued functions of the\nconfiguration (`m_par = ∏ₘ G_{nₘ}(cₘ)`, `m_dau = ∏ₘ G_{n'ₘ}(cₘ)`).\nTheir precise definition is the Hoefsmit/Markov `G`-function product;\nhere they are carried as data so the positivity predicate and the\nexclusion count below are stated over the *actual* products. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.card_config","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.card_config","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L70-L74","doc":"There are `4^A` channel configurations.  (Real, sorry-free fact about\nthe configuration space — the \"out of `4^A`\" half of the count.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Config","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Config","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L66-L68","doc":"A channel configuration for a mass-`A` decay is an assignment of a\n`Channel` to each of the `A` factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.instFintypeChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.instFintypeChannel","kind":"instance","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.instDecidableEqChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.instDecidableEqChannel","kind":"instance","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Channel.sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Channel.sign","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Channel.unconf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Channel.unconf","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Channel.conf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Channel.conf","kind":"ctor","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Channel.triv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Channel.triv","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Channel","kind":"inductive","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean#L57-L64","doc":"The four crossing channels of a single nucleon factor:\ntrivial, confined, unconfined, sign. ","signatureChunk":0}]}